From 36053b65885905c51157d9db5055daeb20735ffb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 12:37:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/46] hydra: translate the bulk of the MaterialX node library

Replaces the chain of ifs with a prefix table, longest match winning, so a
specific variant can sit in front of its family. Two factories cover most of
the volume: one folds every arithmetic node onto math or vector_math with the
mode as a fixed value, the other folds compositing onto mix_color.

Adds roughly seventy nodes: the arithmetic and vector families, compositing
operators, voronoi and white noise procedurals, gradients, bump and
height-to-normal, combine and separate, geometry lookups, and the BSDF, EDF
and VDF closures.

Also routes translation failures through Cycles' logger. They were going to
TF_WARN and TF_RUNTIME_ERROR, which husk swallows - so a node that failed to
map, or a connection dropped for a missing output, was completely silent.
Voronoi was one such case: it has no fac output, its scalar result is
distance, and the dropped connection left a material flat with no indication
why.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
